This project is informed by two GPL-3.0 engines for the same game:

  G-Engine, by Clark Kromenaker - https://github.com/kromenak/gengine
  GK3Reborn                     - https://github.com/Devion/GK3Reborn

The Barn archive layout in crates/barn follows G-Engine's BarnFile.cpp and
GK3Reborn's docs/formats/barn.md. The LZO1X decoder follows the structure of
the reference lzo1x_decompress_safe algorithm.

The rules for when each timeblock ends (crates/game/src/timeblocks.rs) are
G-Engine's reconstruction in its Assets/Timeblocks.shp, restated as Sheep
conditions; the original game keeps them in its executable. Other behaviour
taken from G-Engine (action case ranking, camera collision, conversations,
title cards) is noted where it is implemented. The tables the original
keeps in code rather than data, and that G-Engine reconstructed, are taken
from it too: the fingerprint kit's objects, the driving map's places and
routes, the binoculars' aim, and SIDNEY's files, search events, analyses,
translations, fake IDs and suspects. So are the driving map's hints
(gk3/src/map.rs), from G-Engine's HintManager; CS2's laser heads
(gk3/src/laser_heads.rs), from its LaserHead; TE1's chessboard
(gk3/src/chessboard.rs), from its Chessboard; TE3's pendulum
(gk3/src/pendulum.rs), from its Pendulum; TE6's fight, from its
DemonFight; and its scene functions' mends for faults in the original's
files (MS3, CSE). The score each event is worth
(crates/game/src/scores.rs) and TE5's bridge (gk3/src/bridge.rs) were read
from the original executable.

The Bink decoder (crates/bink) and the Cinepak decoder
(crates/media/src/cinepak.rs) are ports of FFmpeg's bink.c, binkaudio.c,
binkdsp.c and cinepak.c (LGPL-2.1-or-later, https://ffmpeg.org), used here
under the GPL as the LGPL allows.

